# The log of the test must have a line for each of these patterns (grep -E).
# The test controller connects at the first "pad" command.
Gamepad: connected test controller
# Two seconds with the left stick at its full way: 606 units, as with the W key.
\[5\.50\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-415[45] 10431 -259\)
# With the stick at 30% of its way the player gets to the same speed, but later: 536 units.
\[9\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-422[45] 10431 -259\)
# The W key runs as before while the controller is connected.
\[12\.50\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-415[45] 10431 -259\)
# One second of the right stick at its full way turns the view by 197 degrees (35800 of 65536) at each frame rate,
# and 0.3 seconds up give 42 degrees up.
\[14\.60\].* ViewRotation=\(Pitch=0, Yaw=35[78][0-9][0-9], Roll=0\)
\[15\.40\].* ViewRotation=\(Pitch=76[0-9][0-9], Yaw=35[78][0-9][0-9], Roll=0\)
# A jumps.
\[16\.90\].* loc=\(-476[01] 10431 -215\) .* Physics=PHYS_Falling
\[17\.60\].* Physics=PHYS_Walking
# B crouches while it is down.
\[18\.50\].* CollisionHeight=16\.000000 bIsCrouching=True
\[19\.20\].* CollisionHeight=43\.000000 bIsCrouching=False
# LT with LB down uses the binding of the second layer: lean left. The lean stops when LT goes up.
Gamepad: press Joy11 \(layer: LeanLeft\)
\[20\.20\].* curLeanDist=-40\.000000
\[21\.00\].* curLeanDist=0\.000000
